-- Schema drift closure, RLS policies part 3: public schema, tables o-z
-- (45 policies). This completes the policy layer.
--
-- Policy DDL generated by the database from pg_policy, md5-verified against
-- that generated text (19a7b8377a2183aec51f0d137a5bb4c5). DROP POLICY IF
-- EXISTS guards are added for replayability and excluded from verification.
--
-- This batch carries the catalogue visibility chain, which is the single most
-- important rule in the storefront and is repeated consistently across
-- products, variants, inventory and images: a row is visible to anon only
-- when the product is published, active and not soft-deleted AND its producer
-- is active, verified and not soft-deleted. Suspending a producer therefore
-- removes their entire catalogue from public view in one step, with no
-- cascade update and no risk of an orphaned product staying visible.
--
-- Producer self-service is deliberately narrow. A producer may insert, update
-- or delete their own variants and images only while the product sits in
-- draft, review or rejected. Once it is published those paths close, which is
-- what forces edits through the change-request queue rather than letting a
-- published listing be altered silently.
--
-- reviews_insert_verified_purchase is worth reading closely: it requires the
-- review to belong to the caller, to start as pending, to be flagged as a
-- verified purchase, and to reference an order item the caller actually
-- bought on an order that reached delivered or completed. Combined with the
-- UNIQUE constraint on reviews.order_item_id, fake reviews are structurally
-- impossible rather than merely discouraged. reviews_authenticated_update
-- then only permits edits while the review is still pending, so a published
-- review cannot be rewritten after the fact.
--
-- Traceability follows the same discipline: batch rows, batch events and
-- certification links are public only once the batch is released, the parent
-- product is published and the producer is verified, and private batch events
-- stay invisible to anon entirely.
--
-- Applying is a no-op against the live project.

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS orders_authenticated_read ON public.orders;
CREATE POLICY orders_authenticated_read ON public.orders
  FOR SELECT
  TO authenticated
  USING (((user_id = ( SELECT auth.uid() AS uid)) OR ( SELECT private.is_admin() AS is_admin)));

